  "answer": "This has been reported before. The Command Palette dock's performance widgets (CPU, RAM, GPU, network) show ??? with no data. PowerToys#46216 is the main tracking ticket, and a user there reported 0.100.2 still has the problem. PowerToys#46286 was closed as a duplicate of it. No confirmed fix was found in the archive. One user in #46216 got the values back by clicking each widget in the dock. That did not work for others, and it did not help for the related restart-triggered ticket PowerToys#48680. If it still fails, remove the performance monitor band from the dock. A different ticket, PowerToys#48834, says disabling that band avoids a memory leak in it. Please follow #46216 for a fix. You can also add your bug report ZIP and details such as Windows version, CPU and GPU there."
